%description:
TR 38.901 Table 7.4.1-1 gives its urban macrocell path loss for "hBS=25m" and
"1.5m<=hUT<=22.5m". A base station antenna at 30 m is outside it: the formulas would give a
number the study does not stand behind, without a message. The first evaluation of such a link
is an error, unless tolerateHeightViolation is set (AntennaHeight_OutsideStudyRangeTolerated).

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = simu5g.test.moduletest.lib.NrSessionTestNetwork

*.gnb.cellularNic.antenna.mobility.offsetZ = 30m

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%exitcode: 1
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%contains: stderr
the link's base station antenna is at 30 m and its UE antenna at 1.5 m above the ground (z = 0), outside the range TR 38.901 Table 7.4.1-1 gives for the scenario URBAN_MACROCELL (hBS = 25 m, 1.5 m <= hUT <= 22.5 m)
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
